.TH "DEDALUS\-IMAGES\-IMPORT" "1" "" "dedalus" "Dedalus Manual"
.SH "NAME"
dedalus\-images\-import \- Upload an image archive and wait for readiness
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B dedalus images import
.I archive
[options]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Stream a docker save archive to signed storage, register the image, and poll until
ready. Progress is written to stderr and one final image object to stdout.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
.B \-\-name <name>
Image label.
.TP
.B \-\-platform <platform>
linux/amd64 (default and currently supported platform).
.TP
.B \-\-no-wait
Return after upload and registration while preparation continues.
.TP
.B \-\-wait
Wait for readiness (default).
.TP
.B \-\-wait-timeout <seconds>
Total import budget, default 3600. Does not cancel server preparation.
.TP
.B \-\-idempotency-key <key>
Reuse the same key when retrying the same archive and options.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Zero means ready, or accepted when using \-\-no\-wait. Preparation failures exit
nonzero. Ctrl-C exits 130 without deleting an accepted image.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
dedalus(1)
